---
// What "embedded" means, as a shape: the database is inside the process, so a
// read is a function call rather than a round trip.
//
// The comparison animates because the difference is a difference in time. The
// server side sends a packet across a gap and waits; the embedded side does
// not. Running them side by side on the same loop is the argument.
//
// Motion is the point here, so it is not decorative, but it still stops for
// anyone who asked it to: html[data-motion='reduced'] freezes both rows in
// their resting state.
---

<div class="grid gap-px bg-line sm:grid-cols-2">
  <div class="bg-raised p-6">
    <p class="text-small font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-low">Client and server</p>
    <div class="embed-row mt-5 flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="shape-box">app</span>
      <span class="wire"><span class="packet" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
      <span class="shape-box">database</span>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-mid">
      A read leaves the process, crosses a socket, and comes back.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-raised p-6">
    <p class="text-small font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-low">Embedded</p>
    <div class="embed-row mt-5 flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="shape-box shape-outer">
        app
        <span class="shape-inner">strata</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-mid">
      A read is a function call. One directory on disk, no port, nothing to start.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .shape-box {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line-hover);
    border-radius: var(--radius-control);
    padding: 0.625rem 0.875rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-mono-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink-mid);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .shape-outer {
    padding: 0.625rem 0.75rem 0.625rem 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-hi);
  }
  .shape-inner {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-terracotta-700);
    border-radius: var(--radius-control);
    background-color: var(--color-inset);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-terracotta-500);
  }

  /* The gap the packet has to cross, and the packet crossing it. */
  .wire {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    height: 1px;
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 2rem;
    background-color: var(--color-line-hover);
  }
  .packet {
    position: absolute;
    top: -2px;
    left: 0;
    height: 5px;
    width: 5px;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background-color: var(--color-terracotta-500);
    animation: packet 2.4s var(--ease-out) infinite;
  }

  @keyframes packet {
    0% {
      left: 0;
      opacity: 0;
    }
    10% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    45% {
      left: calc(100% - 5px);
      opacity: 1;
    }
    55% {
      left: calc(100% - 5px);
      opacity: 1;
    }
    90% {
      left: 0;
      opacity: 1;
    }
    100% {
      left: 0;
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  html[data-motion='reduced'] .packet {
    animation: none;
    left: calc(50% - 2.5px);
  }
</style>
